          %h3#RelationToGroupExtensions Relation to extensions
          %p
            We discuss how the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ext
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext^n(X,A)
            is identified with the group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensions"} extensions
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^{n-1} A = A[n-1]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            this means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ext
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext^1(X,A)
            classified ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extensions"} group extensions
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            This is the relation that the name “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ext
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext
            ” derives from. At
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group+extension"} infinity-group extension
            is discussed how this relation is a special case of the more general relation that identifies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-spaces"} derived hom-spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(X,\mathbf{B}^{n+1} A)
            with
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h4#1extensions_over_single_objects 1-Extensions over single objects
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,A \in \mathcal{A}
              two objects, an
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to A \to P \to X \to 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of two such extensions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_2
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1 \to P_2
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              fitting into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi P
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi P
                              %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; P_1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp; &amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    A &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp; &amp; \nearrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; P_2
                    }
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              All these homomophisms are necessarily
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+five+lemma"} short five lemma
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ext
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext(X,A)
              for the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of such extensions.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baer+sum"} Baer sum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ext
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ext(X,A)
              becomes an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
          #ExtractCocycleFromExtension.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p Define a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ExtractCocycle
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Extensions
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Ext
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ExtractCocycle
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Extensions(X,A)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Ext^1(X,A)
            %p by the following construction:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Choose a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+presentation"} projective presentation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Q
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \hookrightarrow Q \to X
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to P \to X
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+extension"} extension
                  consider the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi N
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi Q
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi σ
                                      %msub
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                        %mi N
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi σ
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mo =
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi P
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        N
                        \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                        Q
                        \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                        X
                        \\\
                        \\big\downarrow {}^{\mathrlap{\sigma|_N}}
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\big\downarrow {}^{\mathrlap{\sigma}}
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\big\downarrow {}^{\mathrlap{=}}
                        \\\
                        A
                        \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                        P
                        \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                        X
                        }
                        \\,,
                %p where
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                      is any choice of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
                      of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Q
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \to X
                      through
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi P
                              %mo →
                              %mi X
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Q
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
                      is a
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective object
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi N
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma|_N
                      is the induced morphism on the
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exactness
                      of the two sequences.
              %li
                %p
                  By prop.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Ext1FromProjectivePresentation"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma|_N
                  represents an element
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                          %mi σ
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi N
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi Ext
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big[ \sigma|_N \big] \in Ext^1(X,A)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                  of the map to be defined:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ExtractCocycle
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                    %mi σ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ExtractCocycle
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (A \to P \to X)
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    \\big[ \sigma|_N \big]
                    \\,.
            %p
              This construction is independent of the choice of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              involved and hence the map is well-defined.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The map from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExtractCocycleFromExtension"}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              of abelian groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ext
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Ext
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ext(X,A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} Ext^1(X,A)
                    \\,.
